IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `vic-interpretation-time`

-- Tests for vic-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it, before the run.
-- Weekdays were checked against a calendar: 31 Jan 2026 is a Saturday; 16 Jul 2028 is a Sunday; 1 Sep 2030 is a Sunday;
-- 15 Feb 2025 is a Saturday; 28 Feb 2025 is a Friday.

§ `s 44(1) and (2): is the day a period begins or ends on counted?`

-- s 44(1): a period expressed to begin on, or to be reckoned from, a day does not include that day. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1)-(2) the day a period is expressed to begin on or end on is counted in the period` VicBeginsOnDay EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s44(1)-(2) the day a period is expressed to begin on or end on is counted in the period` VicReckonedFromDay EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 44(2): a period expressed to end on, or to be reckoned to, a day includes that day. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1)-(2) the day a period is expressed to begin on or end on is counted in the period` VicEndsOnDay EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s44(1)-(2) the day a period is expressed to begin on or end on is counted in the period` VicReckonedToDay EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The text says nothing about a period "after" or "before" a day. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1)-(2) the day a period is expressed to begin on or end on is counted in the period` VicAfterDay EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s44(1)-(2) the day a period is expressed to begin on or end on is counted in the period` VicBeforeDay EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s44(1) first day counted in a period expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a day` VicReckonedFromDay (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s44(1) first day counted in a period expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a day` VicBeginsOnDay (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s44(1) first day counted in a period expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a day` VicAfterDay (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s44(1) first day counted in a period expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a day` VicEndsOnDay (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s44(2) last day of a period expressed to end on or be reckoned to a day` VicEndsOnDay (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s44(2) last day of a period expressed to end on or be reckoned to a day` VicReckonedToDay (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `s44(2) last day of a period expressed to end on or be reckoned to a day` VicReckonedFromDay (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s44(2) last day of a period expressed to end on or be reckoned to a day` VicAfterDay (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 44(1): periods of days`

-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026: counting starts on 2 January, so the thirtieth day is 31 January. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1) last day of a period of n days reckoned from a day` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 EQUALS Date 31 1 2026
-- One day from 31 December 2025 is 1 January 2026 (across a year end).
#ASSERT `s44(1) last day of a period of n days reckoned from a day` (Date 31 12 2025) 1 EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
-- Across the end of February in a leap year and in a common year.
#ASSERT `s44(1) last day of a period of n days reckoned from a day` (Date 28 2 2024) 1 EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `s44(1) last day of a period of n days reckoned from a day` (Date 28 2 2023) 2 EQUALS Date 2 3 2023
#ASSERT `s44(1) last day of a period of n days reckoned from a day` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 EQUALS Date 1 3 2024
-- Fourteen days from 18 January 2026 ends on 1 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s44(1) last day of a period of n days reckoned from a day` (Date 18 1 2026) 14 EQUALS Date 1 2 2026

#ASSERT `s44 last day of a period counted forward from a day` VicReckonedFromDay 30 VicDays (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s44 last day of a period counted forward from a day` VicBeginsOnDay 30 VicDays (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)

-- A week is not defined in the text, so a period of weeks is not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44 last day of a period counted forward from a day` VicReckonedFromDay 2 VicWeeks (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period "after" a day, or ending on a day, is not covered by this entry point. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44 last day of a period counted forward from a day` VicAfterDay 30 VicDays (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s44 last day of a period counted forward from a day` VicEndsOnDay 30 VicDays (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 44(1), (6)(b), (6)(c): periods of calendar months and years`

-- The two readings, side by side, on the cases the brief names.
-- One month from 15 January 2025: both readings give 15 February 2025.
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading A` (Date 15 1 2025) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 2 2025)
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading B` (Date 15 1 2025) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 2 2025)
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day` (Date 15 1 2025) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 2 2025)

-- One month from 31 January 2024: reading A counts February 2024 whole and ends on 29 February; reading B has no 31 February. The text does not choose. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading A` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading B` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The library's add months clamps to the last day of the shorter month: it gives 29 February 2024. The text does not say that, so the module does not use it.
#ASSERT `add months` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 EQUALS Date 29 2 2024

-- Two months from 31 December 2025: reading A ends 28 February 2026; reading B has no 31 February. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading A` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading B` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 EQUALS NOTHING

-- One month from 28 February 2025, the last day of its month: reading A ends 31 March, reading B ends 28 March. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading A` (Date 28 2 2025) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2025)
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading B` (Date 28 2 2025) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 3 2025)
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day` (Date 28 2 2025) 1 EQUALS NOTHING

-- One month from 30 January 2025: both readings need a day numbered 31 or 30 in February. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day` (Date 30 1 2025) 1 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Years: s 44(6)(c) a year, without qualification, is twelve months.
-- Three years from 16 July 2025 is 16 July 2028 (a Sunday). Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(c) last day of n years reckoned from a day` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 EQUALS JUST (Date 16 7 2028)
-- Five years from 15 January 2025 is 15 January 2030; five years from 1 September 2025 is 1 September 2030 (a Sunday). Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(c) last day of n years reckoned from a day` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(c) last day of n years reckoned from a day` (Date 1 9 2025) 5 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2030)
-- One year from 29 February 2024: reading A ends 28 February 2025, reading B has no 29 February 2025. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading A` (Date 29 2 2024) 12 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading B` (Date 29 2 2024) 12 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(c) last day of n years reckoned from a day` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The library's add years clamps to 28 February 2025; the module does not use it.
#ASSERT `add years` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- One year from 28 February 2023: reading A counts 1 March 2023 to 29 February 2024, reading B ends 28 February 2024. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(c) last day of n years reckoned from a day` (Date 28 2 2023) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- One year from 28 February 2025: both readings give 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s44(1),(6)(c) last day of n years reckoned from a day` (Date 28 2 2025) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)

-- Through the entry point.
#ASSERT `s44 last day of a period counted forward from a day` VicReckonedFromDay 3 VicYears (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 7 2028)
#ASSERT `s44 last day of a period counted forward from a day` VicReckonedFromDay 2 VicCalendarMonths (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s44 last day of a period counted forward from a day` VicBeginsOnDay 1 VicCalendarMonths (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 2 2025)

§ `s 44(3) and (4): a last day that is a holiday`

-- s 44(4)(a): a Saturday or Sunday is a holiday. 31 January 2026 is a Saturday, 1 February a Sunday, 2 February a Monday.
#ASSERT `s44(4) a day is a holiday` (Date 31 1 2026) EMPTY EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s44(4) a day is a holiday` (Date 1 2 2026) EMPTY EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s44(4) a day is a holiday` (Date 2 2 2026) EMPTY EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s44(4) a day is a holiday` (Date 30 1 2026) EMPTY EQUALS FALSE
-- s 44(4)(b): a day appointed under the Public Holidays Act 1993 as a public holiday where the act is to be done. The list is supplied by the caller.
#ASSERT `s44(4) a day is a holiday` (Date 26 1 2026) (LIST (Date 26 1 2026)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s44(4) a day is a holiday` (Date 26 1 2026) EMPTY EQUALS FALSE

-- A last day of Saturday 31 January 2026 extends to the next day that is not a holiday: Monday 2 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (Date 31 1 2026) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- If Monday 2 February is itself a public holiday, the next day that is not a holiday is Tuesday 3 February.
#ASSERT `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (Date 31 1 2026) TRUE (LIST (Date 2 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 2 2026)
-- A last day that is not a holiday is not moved.
#ASSERT `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (Date 30 1 2026) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 30 1 2026)
-- Saturday 15 February 2025 with Monday 17 February a public holiday ends on Tuesday 18 February.
#ASSERT `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (Date 15 2 2025) TRUE (LIST (Date 17 2 2025)) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 2 2025)
-- A time that is not limited for the doing of an act or thing is not within s 44(3). Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (Date 31 1 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

-- The extension applies to a time counted in months or years as well as days: s 44(3) speaks of "the time limited", not of a unit.
-- Three years from 16 July 2025 ends on a Sunday, 16 July 2028, so the time extends to Monday 17 July 2028.
#ASSERT `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (Date 16 7 2028) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 17 7 2028)
-- Five years from 1 September 2025 ends on a Sunday, 1 September 2030, so the time extends to Monday 2 September 2030.
#ASSERT `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (Date 1 9 2030) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 9 2030)
-- Five years from 15 January 2025 ends on Tuesday 15 January 2030, which is not a holiday.
#ASSERT `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (Date 15 1 2030) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026 ends on Saturday 31 January 2026, so the time extends to Monday 2 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (Date 31 1 2026) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)

-- The search for a day that is not a holiday is bounded; at the bound it answers NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s44(3) first day on or after a day that is not a holiday` (Date 31 1 2026) 1 EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s44(3) first day on or after a day that is not a holiday` (Date 31 1 2026) 3 EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
#ASSERT `s44(3) first day on or after a day that is not a holiday` (Date 2 2 2026) 1 EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
#ASSERT `s44(3) first day on or after a day that is not a holiday` (Date 2 2 2026) 0 EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 44(5), (6), (7): standard time, midnight, financial and calendar years, now`

-- s 44(5): the hours standard time runs ahead of Coordinated Universal Time are supplied by the caller (10 in endnote 3 of the text).
#ASSERT `s44(5) hours ahead of Coordinated Universal Time that an expression of time means` 10 FALSE EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `s44(5) hours ahead of Coordinated Universal Time that an expression of time means` 10 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s44(6)(a) midnight in relation to a day is the point at which that day ends` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS VicMoment OF (Date 30 6 2026), VicEndOfDay
#ASSERT `s44(6)(d) midnight at which the financial year ending in a calendar year ends` 2026 EQUALS VicMoment OF (Date 30 6 2026), VicEndOfDay
#ASSERT `s44(6)(d) first day of the financial year ending on 30 June of a year` 2026 EQUALS Date 1 7 2025
#ASSERT `s44(6)(e) midnight at which a calendar year ends` 2025 EQUALS VicMoment OF (Date 31 12 2025), VicEndOfDay
#ASSERT `s44(6)(e) first day of the calendar year ending on 31 December of a year` 2025 EQUALS Date 1 1 2025
#ASSERT `s44(7) the time that now, heretofore and hereafter refer to` (VicMoment OF (Date 1 7 1984), VicBeginningOfDay) EQUALS VicMoment OF (Date 1 7 1984), VicBeginningOfDay

§ `ss 10A, 11, 12, 24 and 25: coming into operation, passing and expiry`

-- A day fixed in the Act itself: the Act comes into operation at the beginning of that day (s 11(1)).
#ASSERT `s11 moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a fixed day` (Date 1 7 1984) FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST (VicInOperationFrom (VicMoment OF (Date 1 7 1984), VicBeginningOfDay))
-- A day fixed by a proclamation that is not yet published: publication is a condition precedent (s 11(2)).
#ASSERT `s11 moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a fixed day` (Date 1 7 2027) TRUE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST VicNotYetInOperation
-- Published before the fixed day: the beginning of the fixed day (s 11(1)).
#ASSERT `s11 moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a fixed day` (Date 1 7 2027) TRUE (JUST (Date 20 6 2027)) TRUE EQUALS JUST (VicInOperationFrom (VicMoment OF (Date 1 7 2027), VicBeginningOfDay))
-- Published on the fixed day itself: the beginning of the fixed day.
#ASSERT `s11 moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a fixed day` (Date 1 7 2027) TRUE (JUST (Date 1 7 2027)) TRUE EQUALS JUST (VicInOperationFrom (VicMoment OF (Date 1 7 2027), VicBeginningOfDay))
-- Made on or before the fixed day but published after it: the beginning of the day of publication (s 11(2A)).
#ASSERT `s11 moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a fixed day` (Date 1 7 2027) TRUE (JUST (Date 2 7 2027)) TRUE EQUALS JUST (VicInOperationFrom (VicMoment OF (Date 2 7 2027), VicBeginningOfDay))
-- Made after the fixed day and published after it: s 11(2A) does not apply and no section says. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s11 moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a fixed day` (Date 1 7 2027) TRUE (JUST (Date 2 7 2027)) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s11(3) date of the passing of an Act` (Date 22 5 1984) EQUALS Date 22 5 1984

#ASSERT `s11(4) date of commencement of an Act or portion whose provisions began on different days` (LIST (Date 1 3 2020), Date 1 7 2021, Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2021)
#ASSERT `s11(4) date of commencement of an Act or portion whose provisions began on different days` (LIST (Date 1 3 2020)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2020)
#ASSERT `s11(4) date of commencement of an Act or portion whose provisions began on different days` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 10A: passed 15 May 2024, the first anniversary is 15 May 2025.
#ASSERT `s10A first anniversary of the passing of an Act` (Date 15 5 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 5 2025)
-- Passed 29 February 2024: no section says what the anniversary is. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s10A first anniversary of the passing of an Act` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s10A(3),(4) day an Act with no commencement provision is taken to come into operation` (Date 15 5 2024) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 15 5 2025)
-- A day proclaimed before the anniversary is the earlier.
#ASSERT `s10A(3),(4) day an Act with no commencement provision is taken to come into operation` (Date 15 5 2024) (JUST (Date 1 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2025)
-- A day proclaimed after the anniversary is not the earlier.
#ASSERT `s10A(3),(4) day an Act with no commencement provision is taken to come into operation` (Date 15 5 2024) (JUST (Date 1 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 5 2025)
-- A day proclaimed on the anniversary itself.
#ASSERT `s10A(3),(4) day an Act with no commencement provision is taken to come into operation` (Date 15 5 2024) (JUST (Date 15 5 2025)) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 5 2025)
#ASSERT `s10A(3),(4) day an Act with no commencement provision is taken to come into operation` (Date 29 2 2024) (JUST (Date 1 1 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 12 and s 25: until the last moment of the day.
#ASSERT `s12 moment until which a temporary Act or provision continues in operation` (Date 30 6 2030) EQUALS VicMoment OF (Date 30 6 2030), VicLastMomentOfDay
#ASSERT `s25 moment until which a temporary subordinate instrument or provision continues in operation` (Date 30 6 2030) EQUALS VicMoment OF (Date 30 6 2030), VicLastMomentOfDay
-- s 24: beginning of the fixed day, unless the instrument is a statutory rule (which the section leaves out).
#ASSERT `s24 moment a subordinate instrument that is not a statutory rule comes into operation` (Date 1 7 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST (VicMoment OF (Date 1 7 2027), VicBeginningOfDay)
#ASSERT `s24 moment a subordinate instrument that is not a statutory rule comes into operation` (Date 1 7 2027) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 49: service by post`

#ASSERT `s49 service by post is deemed effected` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s49 service by post is deemed effected` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s49 service by post is deemed effected` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s49 service by post is deemed effected` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s49 service by post is deemed effected` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s49 day on which service by post is deemed effected` VicOrdinaryPost (Date 12 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 12 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s49 day on which service by post is deemed effected` VicRegisteredPostOrCertifiedMail (Date 11 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s49 day on which service by post is deemed effected` VicOrdinaryPost (Date 12 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s49 day on which service by post is deemed effected` VicRegisteredPostOrCertifiedMail (Date 11 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `the dates the Act names`

#ASSERT `s2 day the Act came into operation` EQUALS Date 1 7 1984
#ASSERT `s9(2)(e) last day of the period in which an Act is cited by its number only` EQUALS Date 31 12 1985
#ASSERT `s9(2)(f) first day of the period in which an Act is cited by year and number` EQUALS Date 1 1 1986
#ASSERT `s10(3) first day on which an Act passed without a short title leaves its long title out of the Act` EQUALS Date 1 9 1985
#ASSERT `s21(1) day on which Imperial and New South Wales Acts are read as references to Victoria` EQUALS Date 1 7 1851
#ASSERT `s21(2) day on which an Act is read as referring to the Legislative Council of Victoria` EQUALS Date 21 11 1856
#ASSERT `s36 first day of the period in which headings, examples, notes, diagrams and punctuation form part of an Act` EQUALS Date 1 1 2001
#ASSERT `s38AA(2) day Standards Australia took over from the Standards Association of Australia` EQUALS Date 1 7 1999
#ASSERT `s38EA(2) first day on which registered medical practitioner is defined` EQUALS Date 1 7 2015
#ASSERT `s55(2)(a) day before which the three months are counted` EQUALS Date 26 1 1984
#ASSERT `s64B(1) first day of the period of a purported appointment` EQUALS Date 3 3 1986

§ `s 55(2): three months and eighteen years`

-- Three months immediately before 26 January 1984 begin on 26 October 1983 and end on 25 January 1984.
#ASSERT `s44(6)(b) first day of n calendar months ending immediately before a day` (Date 26 1 1984) 3 EQUALS JUST (Date 26 10 1983)
-- Where the two readings differ the text does not choose. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s44(6)(b) first day of n calendar months ending immediately before a day` (Date 1 3 2025) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s44(6)(b) first day of n calendar months ending immediately before a day` (Date 31 3 2025) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A person born on 25 January 1966 reached 18 on 25 January 1984, before 26 January 1984: so did not satisfy "had not attained".
#ASSERT `s55(2) day on which a person born on a day reaches eighteen years, taken as the eighteenth anniversary` (Date 25 1 1966) EQUALS JUST (Date 25 1 1984)
#ASSERT `s55(2)(b) had not attained the full age of 18 years before 26 January 1984` (Date 25 1 1966) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Born on 26 January 1966: 18 on 26 January 1984, which is not before that date.
#ASSERT `s55(2)(b) had not attained the full age of 18 years before 26 January 1984` (Date 26 1 1966) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s55(2)(b) had not attained the full age of 18 years before 26 January 1984` (Date 27 1 1966) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Born on a 29 February: no section says on which day the age is attained in a year without one. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `s55(2)(b) had not attained the full age of 18 years before 26 January 1984` (Date 29 2 1968) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 64B(1): the period of a purported appointment`

-- Endnote 2 gives 10.12.25 for the commencement of section 61 of Act No. 55/2025, which inserted s 64A.
#ASSERT `endnote 2 day sections 57, 58, 60 and 61 of Act No. 55/2025 came into operation` EQUALS Date 10 12 2025
-- The period ends immediately before s 64A came into operation: on 9 December 2025.
#ASSERT `s64B(1) last day of the period of a purported appointment` (Date 10 12 2025) EQUALS Date 9 12 2025
#ASSERT `s64B(1) last day of the period of a purported appointment` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- An appointment made on 3 March 1986 is within the period; one made on 2 March 1986 is not; the last day is 9 December 2025, and 10 December 2025 is not within the period.
#ASSERT `s64B(1) the appointment was made during the period of a purported appointment` (Date 3 3 1986) (Date 10 12 2025) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s64B(1) the appointment was made during the period of a purported appointment` (Date 2 3 1986) (Date 10 12 2025) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s64B(1) the appointment was made during the period of a purported appointment` (Date 9 12 2025) (Date 10 12 2025) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s64B(1) the appointment was made during the period of a purported appointment` (Date 10 12 2025) (Date 10 12 2025) EQUALS FALSE
